# Template for `.env`, which holds local secrets and deployment-local overrides
# and is gitignored (`*.env`). Copy to `.env` and fill in the values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing loads this file implicitly. `just run-dev` runs the service with it
# (`dotenv -f .env run just run`, needs the dotenv CLI); `just run` and every
# other recipe ignore it. That is deliberate: `set dotenv-load := true` is global
# in just, and a globally loaded `.env` also reaches `just test`, where an
# INTERCHAIN_INDEXER_CHAINS__* override lands on the offline fixture and fails
# the typed load.
#
# Nothing here is required either: no config file under `config/` declares an
# `api_key`, so the service starts without any key. A credential is opt-in and
# lives here in full — the `api_key` object declaring its *shape*, and the
# INTERCHAIN_INDEXER_RPC_API_KEY__* variable holding its *value*. Declare both or
# neither: a declared `api_key` whose value is unset, empty or whitespace-only
# fails startup, naming the chain, the provider and the exact variable.
#
# Value variable: INTERCHAIN_INDEXER_RPC_API_KEY__<CHAIN_ID>__<PROVIDER>
# (provider uppercased, every character outside [A-Z0-9_] replaced by `_`),
# or whatever `api_key.value_env` names instead. See config/ENVs.md.

# Optional, for config/full-mainnet: chain 8021 (NUMINE Mainnet), provider
# "glacier". Glacier rate-limits harder without a key; raising MAX_RPS above the
# file's `1` usually goes with it. Uncomment all three, or none.
# INTERCHAIN_INDEXER_CHAINS__8021__RPCS__GLACIER__API_KEY__LOCATION=header
# INTERCHAIN_INDEXER_CHAINS__8021__RPCS__GLACIER__API_KEY__PARAM_NAME=x-glacier-api-key
# INTERCHAIN_INDEXER_RPC_API_KEY__8021__GLACIER=
